ENTIFIERS><DESCRIPTOR><STUDY_TITLE>Molecular responses and metabolic reset of apple fruit under postharvest low oxygen stress</STUDY_TITLE><STUDY_TYPE existing_study_type="Transcriptome Analysis"/><STUDY_ABSTRACT>In the present work we report data on the application of an integrated approach on apples held under two levels of low oxygen concentrations  throughout  the initial 2 months of  storage, when, in general, strict control of the effects of the extremely low oxygen concentration is  required for a successful DCA performance. Overall design: Examination of 4 different condition. Three replicates per condition</STUDY_ABSTRACT><CENTER_PROJECT_NAME>GSE72153</CENTER_PROJECT_NAME></DESCRIPTOR><STUDY_LINKS><STUDY_LINK><XREF_LINK><DB>pubmed</DB><ID>26909091</ID></XREF_LINK></STUDY_LINK></STUDY_LINKS></STUDY><SAMPLE alias="GSM1856252" accession="SRS1038518"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRS1038518</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioSample">SAMN03998551</EXTERNAL_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="GEO">GSM1856252</EXTERNAL_ID></IDENTIFIERS><TITLE>Sample collected aftershift from 0.4 kPa ox to 0.8 kPa ox</TITLE><SAMPLE_NAME><TAXON_ID>3750</TAXON_ID><SCIENTIFIC_NAME>Malus domestica</SCIENTIFIC_NAME></SAMPLE_NAME><SAMPLE_LINKS><SAMPLE_LINK><XREF_LINK><DB>bioproject</DB><ID>293208</ID><LABEL>PRJNA293208</LABEL></XREF_LINK></SAMPLE_LINK></SAMPLE_LINKS><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTES><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>source_name</TAG><VALUE>Slices (about 1 cm thick) of cortex tissue from the equatorial part of fruit</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>cultivar</TAG><VALUE>Granny Smith</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>tissue</TAG><VALUE>cortex</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTES></SAMPLE><Pool><Member member_name="" accession="SRS1038518" sample_name="GSM1856252" sample_title="Sample collected aftershift from 0.4 kPa ox to 0.8 kPa ox" spots="38757519" bases="1896036636" tax_id="3750" organism="Malus domestica"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRS1038518</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID