ke Tims Branch ideal for studying ironoxidizers. This project is designed to fill research gaps surrounding the rate and controls on environmentaliron oxidation, and the metabolism of FeOB.The research objectives are:Objective 1: Quantify microbial iron oxidation rates in terrestrial iron mats using an integratedfield and kinetics studyObjective 2: Identify and quantify dominant iron-oxidizing microorganisms in terrestrialiron mats using metagenomics and metatranscriptomicsObjective 3: Construct microbial metabolic models of iron oxidizers and iron matcommunities to link microbial iron oxidation to C, N and S cycling</STUDY_ABSTRACT></DESCRIPTOR><STUDY_LINKS><STUDY_LINK><XREF_LINK><DB>pubmed</DB><ID>39133000</ID></XREF_LINK></STUDY_LINK></STUDY_LINKS></STUDY><SAMPLE alias="2105MN1" accession="SRS21513452"><IDENTIFIERS><PRIMARY_ID>SRS21513452</PRIMARY_ID><EXTERNAL_ID namespace="BioSample">SAMN41570335</EXTERNAL_ID><SUBMITTER_ID namespace="pda|gtothero@orcid" label="Sample name">2105MN1</SUBMITTER_ID></IDENTIFIERS><SAMPLE_NAME><TAXON_ID>527640</TAXON_ID><SCIENTIFIC_NAME>microbial mat metagenome</SCIENTIFIC_NAME></SAMPLE_NAME><SAMPLE_LINKS><SAMPLE_LINK><XREF_LINK><DB>bioproject</DB><ID>1117470</ID><LABEL>PRJNA1117470</LABEL></XREF_LINK></SAMPLE_LINK></SAMPLE_LINKS><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTES><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>collection_date</TAG><VALUE>2021-05-17</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>depth</TAG><VALUE>35</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>elev</TAG><VALUE>260</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>env_broad_scale</TAG><VALUE>freshwater terrestrial wetland</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>env_local_scale</TAG><VALUE>iron microbial mat</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>env_medium</TAG><VALUE>iron microbial mat</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>geo_loc_name</TAG><VALUE>USA: South Carolina, Savannah River Site</VALUE></SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><SAMPLE_ATTRIBUTE><TAG>lat_lon</TAG><VALUE>33.34 N 81.72 W</V